==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|enm|not}}, {{m|enm|nat}}, variant of {{m|enm|noght}}, {{m|enm|naht||not, nothing}}, from {{der|en|ang|*nōht}}, {{m|ang|nāht||nought, nothing}}, short for {{m|ang|nōwiht}}, {{m|ang|nāwiht||nothing|lit=not anything}}, corresponding to {{m|ang|ne||not}} + {{m|ang|ōwiht}}, {{m|ang|āwiht||anything}}, corresponding to {{m|ang|ā||ever, always}} + {{m|ang|wiht||thing, creature}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|nat}}, {{m|sco|naucht||not}}, {{cog|stq|nit||not}}, {{cog|fy|net||not}}, {{cog|nl|niet||not}}, {{cog|de|nicht||not}}. Compare {{l|en|nought}}, {{l|en|naught}} and {{l|en|aught}}. More at {{m|en|no}}, {{m|en|wight}}, {{m|en|whit}}.

